WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.248 --> 00:00:02.305
- Dear Journal, it's me Doug.

00:00:02.305 --> 00:00:04.216
- I may not be the President,

00:00:04.216 --> 00:00:05.379
- Yeah.

00:00:05.379 --> 00:00:06.861
- Quiet!

00:00:06.861 --> 00:00:08.067
(upbeat music)

00:00:08.067 --> 00:00:09.804
- On Nickelodeon in the '90s,

00:00:09.804 --> 00:00:11.725
I was the voice of Doug Funnie,

00:00:11.725 --> 00:00:14.142
Roger Klotz, Ren, and Stimpy.

00:00:18.147 --> 00:00:19.832
What a decade.

00:00:19.832 --> 00:00:22.415
(upbeat music)

00:00:24.632 --> 00:00:27.722
I put a tiny little bit of my own self

00:00:27.722 --> 00:00:29.505
into each character.

00:00:29.505 --> 00:00:30.657
- [Interviewer] Give me a Doug Funnie.

00:00:30.657 --> 00:00:32.886
- Hi everybody, this is Doug Funnie.

00:00:32.886 --> 00:00:36.769
Uh, I got such a crush
on Patti Mayonnaise.

00:00:36.769 --> 00:00:39.328
I was pretty much like
that at 11 years old.

00:00:39.328 --> 00:00:41.580
I used to fantasize a lot, you know,

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:43.585
I could entertain myself for hours.

00:00:43.585 --> 00:00:44.940
- [Interviewer] And what about Roger?

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:47.041
- Hey, you're the biggest loser I ever saw!

00:00:47.041 --> 00:00:48.374
(laughs)

00:00:48.374 --> 00:00:51.883
He was based on a bully
that used to bother me.

00:00:51.883 --> 00:00:53.151
- [Interviewer] How about Ren?

00:00:53.151 --> 00:00:55.148
- Will you shut up, you fool!

00:00:55.148 --> 00:00:56.758
Else I shall kill you!

00:00:56.758 --> 00:00:57.610
- [Interviewer] And Stimpy?

00:00:57.610 --> 00:00:59.668
- Hey Ren, I picked a nose goblin.

00:00:59.668 --> 00:01:01.251
I picked it myself.

00:01:02.102 --> 00:01:03.125
Pew!

00:01:03.125 --> 00:01:04.406
- [Interviewer] Do you
still entertain yourself?

00:01:04.406 --> 00:01:05.845
- I'm sick of myself.

00:01:05.845 --> 00:01:07.766
(laughs)

00:01:07.766 --> 00:01:10.326
- [Interviewer] You also
do Futurama, Philip J. Fry.

00:01:10.326 --> 00:01:12.289
- Man, all this constant
exposure to radiation

00:01:12.289 --> 00:01:13.772
is making me thirsty.

00:01:13.772 --> 00:01:15.404
Shut up and take my money!

00:01:15.404 --> 00:01:17.644
I sounded just like that when I was 25.

00:01:17.644 --> 00:01:19.564
I was all whiny and nasally.

00:01:19.564 --> 00:01:22.273
If I broke a string on stage, you know, it's like,

00:01:22.273 --> 00:01:24.193
ah man, what am I gonna do now?

00:01:24.193 --> 00:01:25.418
- [Interviewer] And Dr. Zoidberg?

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:28.096
- Young lady, bring me a
sandwich from the dumpster.

00:01:28.096 --> 00:01:29.473
And leave the maggots on it.

00:01:29.473 --> 00:01:30.306
Wooooo!

00:01:31.148 --> 00:01:34.593
(claws clapping)

00:01:34.593 --> 00:01:35.734
I'm struggling.

00:01:35.734 --> 00:01:36.748
- [Interviewer] Professor Farnsworth?

00:01:36.748 --> 00:01:38.518
- Good news everyone.

00:01:38.518 --> 00:01:41.665
I don't want to live on
this planet any more.

00:01:41.665 --> 00:01:42.902
- [Interviewer] Zapp Brannigan?

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:44.470
- She's a beautiful ship, alright.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:47.393
I'm gonna fly her brains out.

00:01:47.393 --> 00:01:50.860
I'm very fortunate, really
lucky that I can do what I do,

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:52.342
and I want to just keep coming to work

00:01:52.342 --> 00:01:54.326
until they tell me don't come in anymore.

00:01:54.326 --> 00:01:56.714
And as a final word, mwah!

00:01:56.714 --> 00:01:57.547
Goodbye.

00:01:59.072 --> 00:02:01.655
(upbeat music)

